{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-28", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curve (roll film, ILFORD ID-11 stock, 8.5 min, 20 C, intermittent agitation) and spectral sensitivity digitised from the Ilford data sheet (DELTA 100 Professional technical information, April 2023, pages 1, 4 and 5). Original data are property of Harman technology Limited (Ilford). The data sheet gives relative log exposure only: the exposure axis was anchored so that the speed point (density = fog + 0.1) lies at log10(0.8/ISO 100) lux-s, and shifted by -0.84 log lux-s so that 0 is the mid-grey exposure at box speed. Sensitivity offset chosen so that mid-grey renders at the reference level; sensitivity is the sheet's relative (linear) wedge-spectrogram curve under tungsten light, used as given. Tail above the sheet range extrapolated with decaying slope. Single development time (the sheet shows one curve). ", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format and wavelength grid taken from spektrafilm. grain_scale is an ESTIMATE (no data sheet value): target RMS granularity 8 assumed from the film class (similar to Kodak T-MAX / Tri-X class); simulated value at density 1.0 was 13.7 before scaling."}, "info": {"stock": "ilford_delta_100", "name": "Ilford Delta 100 Professional Black and White Negative Film, ID-11", "type": "negative", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "strong", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "bw", "densitometer": "diffuse_visual", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "grain_scale": 0.584, "default_look": {"paper_grade": 3.0, "paper_gamma": 1.05, "print_ev": -0.05, "paper": "ilford_multigrade_iv_rc", "taking_filter": "gelb15", "taking_filter_amount": 0.2}, "card": {"maker": "Ilford", "iso": 100, "type": "Schwarzwei\u00dfnegativfilm (Tabular-Korn)", "rms": null, "additional": "Datenblatt (ohne Zahlenwerte)", "text": "Sehr feines Korn, hohe Sch\u00e4rfe und klare Zeichnung. Moderner Look mit kr\u00e4ftigen Mittelt\u00f6nen.", "source": "Ilford Delta 100", "process": "Schwarzwei\u00df-Negativentwicklung", "period": "eingef\u00fchrt 1992; wird hergestellt", "suitable": ["Landschaft und Architektur", "Studio und Stillleben", "feine Vergr\u00f6\u00dferungen"], "less_suitable": ["schnelle Action", "schlechtes Licht"], "tips": ["Aufnahmefilter Gr\u00fcn (11): Der Look \u201eAbgestimmt\u201c legt ihn bereits mit etwa 50 % davor (Haut beh\u00e4lt Tiefe, Laub wird heller); \u201eKeiner\u201c oder \u201eDatenblatt\u201c zeigt die rohe Wiedergabe.", "Filmlooks \u201eDelta 100 \u00b7 fein\u201c (Papiergrad 3) und \u201eDelta 100 \u00b7 hart\u201c (Grad 4) f\u00fcr klare, kr\u00e4ftige Abz\u00fcge."], "facts": [{"text": "Delta 100 und 400 kamen 1992 als Tabular-Korn-Filme von Ilford auf den Markt, als Gegenst\u00fcck zu Kodaks T-Max. Ilford empfiehlt Delta 100 als Ersatz f\u00fcr Agfa APX 100.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilford_Delta"}, {"text": "Das Datenblatt nennt Delta 100 einen mittelschnellen, feink\u00f6rnigen Film f\u00fcr Bild- und Kunstfotografie (ISO 100/21\u00b0).", "source": "Ilford Delta 100 Professional, Technical Information (2023)"}]}, "grain_size_